// Instance discovery and "who am I" for the Loams apps (design §37 §8.2,
// AP0 Task 1).
//
// `GetInstance` needs no credentials: an app calls it first, before sign-in,
// to learn what this instance is, which API packages it serves and where to
// sign in. It mirrors the console's `GET /api/v1/instance` (§19 §3) and adds
// what the desktop and phones need: the OAuth issuer and JWKS, the TLS pin
// set for paired phones, push configuration and minimum app versions.
//
// Rules shared by every app-facing package (AP0 Rulings 2–6): unary and
// server-streaming RPCs only; every RPC has its own request and response
// message; idempotent reads are marked NO_SIDE_EFFECTS so Connect clients
// may send them as HTTP GET; every mutation takes an `idempotency_key`;
// errors carry a `loams.errors.v1.ErrorInfo` with a stable `reason`.

